# This machine's own git settings, not in the dotfiles repo. chezmoi creates this file once and never changes it.
#
# `git config --global` writes here (git's rule: to ~/.gitconfig whenever it exists), so settings that tools
# save for this machine - `gh auth setup-git`'s credential helper, Git LFS, an IDE's merge tool - stay here
# instead of landing in the shared, public ~/.config/git/config. Git reads this file after that one, so a
# setting here overrides the shared one on this machine only.
#
# A setting every machine should have: put it in the repo (home/dot_config/git/config) and delete it here.
